  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$\n- $[-1,1]$\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-1,1]$ is closed. The boundary points are $-1$, and $1.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$ has a boundary point $0$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
